  "question": {
    "text": "A massless rod $B D$ is suspended by two identical massless strings $A B$ and $C D$ of equal lengths. A block of mass ' $m$ ' is suspended point $P$ such that $B P$ is equal to ' $x$ ', if the fundamental frequency of the left wire is twice the fundamental frequency of right wire, then the value of $x$ is\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/kFubdTzCAp7Sxepzvw02bmX6QUSOvEenKMtjcCm52SA.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
